From: Yusuf İhsan KILINÇ
Subject: [PATCH 0090] wsi: native images without dma-buf export on devices that have none

On top of 0089 (src/mesa-cts1, build-cts1, same meson options as build-prod8). NOT installed.

A headless swapchain (VK_EXT_headless_surface) of a hardware device uses native DRM images
(wsi_configure_native_image / wsi_create_native_image_mem): the image is created with
VkExternalMemoryImageCreateInfo(DMA_BUF), its memory allocated exportable as DMA_BUF and exported at once
(wsi_init_image_dmabuf_fd -> vkGetMemoryFdKHR). With xemac (macOS: no dma-bufs, no
VK_EXT_external_memory_dma_buf) the export fails in ANV (anv_device_export_bo: anv_gem_handle_to_fd < 0 ->
VK_ERROR_TOO_MANY_OBJECTS), so every headless vkCreateSwapchainKHR failed:
dEQP-VK.image.swapchain_mutable.headless.* (90 fails) and dEQP-VK.api.array.oversized_array.wsi.headless.* (5).

wsi_device now records VK_EXT_external_memory_dma_buf support (has_export_memory_dma_buf). Without it a native
image is created and allocated without the DMA_BUF external handle type and not exported: image->dma_buf_fd
stays -1, which the acquire/present paths already treat as "no dma-buf implicit sync" (as when the kernel
lacks sync-file import/export). Headless never reads its images outside the device, so it works unchanged,
with the same tiled, modifier-selected, blit-free images as on Linux. The window systems that do share
images (X11, Wayland, display) are not built without dma-bufs, and every Linux driver using this path exposes
VK_EXT_external_memory_dma_buf, so nothing changes there.

Not chosen: CPU images for such devices (WSI_IMAGE_TYPE_CPU, what MESA_VK_WSI_DEBUG=sw does). It also creates
the swapchains, but adds an image-to-buffer blit per present and records command buffers during
vkCreateSwapchainKHR, which crashes dEQP-VK.wsi.headless.swapchain.simulate_oom.* (SIGSEGV in ANV's
mi_builder/blorp writing into the NULL dwords of a batch whose allocation failed; reproducible on prod8 with
MESA_VK_WSI_DEBUG=sw).

Generated-by: LLM

diff --git a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common.c b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common.c
index b1d9658..d8af8b8 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common.c
@@ -172,6 +172,8 @@ wsi_device_init(struct wsi_device *wsi,
       &vk_physical_device_from_handle(pdevice)->supported_extensions;
    wsi->has_import_memory_host =
       supported_extensions->EXT_external_memory_host;
+   wsi->has_export_memory_dma_buf =
+      supported_extensions->EXT_external_memory_dma_buf;
    wsi->has_present_wait = supported_extensions->KHR_present_wait ||
                            supported_extensions->KHR_present_wait2;
 
diff --git a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common.h b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common.h
